# ── (Removed) legacy redirect shim for old API paths ──────────────────────────
# A previous version of this file rewrote old function paths to /api/* with a
# 200-status rewrite. Cloudflare Pages doesn't reliably proxy POST requests
# through that kind of rewrite (confirmed live: it returned a bare 405 with
# no body instead of forwarding the request — that's what broke the AI
# article button, escrow release, and withdrawal requests). All frontend code
# now calls /api/payment, /api/ai-generate, /api/sitemap-dynamic etc. directly,
# so no shim is needed — deleting it instead of leaving a trap for the next
# edit that forgets and calls an old path again.
# /sitemap-live.xml is now served directly by functions/sitemap-live.xml.js
# (the old 200-rewrite to /api/sitemap-dynamic returned 404 on Pages).

# Blog routes
/blog /blog/index.html 200
/blog/ /blog/index.html 200

# Article slugs
/blog/افضل-خدمات-رقمية-في-مصر-2025 /blog/افضل-خدمات-رقمية-في-مصر-2025/index.html 200
/blog/بوابات-الدفع-الالكتروني-مصر /blog/بوابات-الدفع-الالكتروني-مصر/index.html 200
/blog/كيفية-الربح-من-الانترنت-مصر /blog/كيفية-الربح-من-الانترنت-مصر/index.html 200
/blog/تحسين-محركات-البحث-للمواقع-العربية /blog/تحسين-محركات-البحث-للمواقع-العربية/index.html 200
/blog/التجارة-الالكترونية-في-مصر /blog/التجارة-الالكترونية-في-مصر/index.html 200
/blog/freelancing-egypt-2025 /blog/freelancing-egypt-2025/index.html 200
/blog/digital-marketing-arabic /blog/digital-marketing-arabic/index.html 200
/blog/escrow-payment-protection /blog/escrow-payment-protection/index.html 200
/blog/web-design-trends-2025 /blog/web-design-trends-2025/index.html 200
/blog/paymob-instapay-guide /blog/paymob-instapay-guide/index.html 200

# Old blog sitemap (replaced by the live sitemap that also lists the hand-written articles): keep old submissions working.
/blog-sitemap.xml /sitemap-live.xml 301

# Dynamic (AI) articles: /blog/:slug is handled by functions/blog/[slug].js (route enabled in _routes.json).
# It returns a REAL 404 for unknown slugs and injects canonical/og/JSON-LD per article. The old blanket rule
# "/blog/:slug /blog/index.html 200" was removed on purpose: it answered 200 for every slug (soft 404).

# Legacy standalone legal pages — superseded by the redesigned /terms and
# /privacy folders below. Kept as 301s (not deleted) so old bookmarks/backlinks
# and any URL already indexed by Google land on the current page instead of
# a stale duplicate with an outdated design (was previously reachable and
# linked from index.html's footer/signup-modal by mistake — now fixed to
# point at /terms and /privacy directly, this redirect is the safety net).
/terms.html /terms 301
/privacy.html /privacy 301
/refund-policy.html /refund-policy 301

# Static pages
/about /about/index.html 200
/about/ /about/index.html 200
/contact /contact/index.html 200
/contact/ /contact/index.html 200
/privacy /privacy/index.html 200
/privacy/ /privacy/index.html 200
/terms /terms/index.html 200
/terms/ /terms/index.html 200
/refund-policy /refund-policy/index.html 200
/refund-policy/ /refund-policy/index.html 200

# No SPA catch-all on purpose.
# The app uses HASH routing (/#services, /#store-<id> …) and every real path it links to exists as a file or a
# Function (/, /about, /blog, /contact, /privacy, /terms, /refund-policy, /api/*, /sitemap-live.xml). A blanket
# "/* /index.html 200" answered 200 for ANY made-up URL (soft 404 for Google). Unknown paths now get the real
# 404 page (404.html, status 404). If real path-based app URLs are introduced one day, add explicit rules for them.
